# Every consumer of this repository reads these files on a POSIX system: the
# CI runner, the hosted notebook, and the compute nodes, which receive shell
# scripts copied straight out of a working tree. A CRLF line ending reaches
# bash as part of the last word on the line, so `set -euo pipefail` becomes a
# request for an option named "pipefail\r" and the script dies on its first
# statement. Line endings are LF in the repository and in every working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.parquet binary
